NAME
    coretop - live hardware dashboard of the loaded core (stub in module ABI)

SYNOPSIS
    coretop [-w]

DESCRIPTION
    Intended to display an auto-refreshing, htop-style dashboard of the
    attached core's hardware telemetry (per-subsystem load bars, CPU
    registers, sprite capacity, audio channels, palette, and VRAM preview).

    In the current emusen.session module implementation, 'coretop' is a
    refusal stub: it verifies that a session is attached and then returns
    an error because module commands run over buffered output and cannot
    drive a raw interactive terminal or open a frontend window directly.

    Use summary(1), regs(1), sprites(1), channels(1), pal(1), and
    counters(1) to inspect session state from the shell.

OPTIONS
    -w
        Request a separate frontend window. Currently fails with
        "coretop: -w is not supported by this frontend."

EXAMPLES
    coretop
    coretop -w

EXIT STATUS
    1   Always fails in the current module implementation (no session
        attached, no interactive terminal, or windowed mode unsupported).

SEE ALSO
    summary(1), regs(1), sprites(1), channels(1), pal(1), counters(1),
    profile(1)
